      "sentence_id": 1,
      "japanese": "人は一人か二人しか乗れないし、荷物もたくさん載せられない。",
      "english_translation": "It can only carry one or two people, and it cannot carry much luggage."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 2,
      "japanese": "そのような不便で、「特別な」乗り物に乗っているライダー同士の、不思議な仲間意識というものがある。",
      "english_translation": "There's this strange sense of camaraderie that exists between riders who share a unique, inconvenient mode of transportation."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 3,
      "japanese": "初めて会った人が自分と同じ趣味だったので、すぐに仲良くなれたという経験は、誰にでもあるだろう。",
      "english_translation": "I had an experience where I quickly became friends with someone I met for the first time because we shared the same interests. This is likely something many people can relate to."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 4,
      "japanese": "それと同じで、趣味としてのバイクは、仲間意識を作りやすい。",
      "english_translation": "Similarly, having a motorcycle as a hobby can foster a sense of camaraderie among riders."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 5,
      "japanese": "しかも、他の趣味とはちょっと違う形で。",
      "english_translation": "Also, it's different from other hobbies in a unique way."
